<title>JAPAN: Takeda Chemical sets up British subisidiary.</title>
<headline>Takeda Chemical sets up British subisidiary.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Takeda Chemical Industries Ltd said on Friday that it had set up a wholly owned subsidiary in Britain to market its drugs.</p>
<p>The new firm was set up on April 25 with starting capital of 12 million pounds.</p>
<p>The company will market Takeda's hypertension medicine, TCV-116, as well as diabetes drugs AO-128 and AD-4833, Takeda said in a statement.</p>
</text>
